## 3. Absolute counts without an observed eligible denominator

Select **cvap_exposure_count_v1** where the legal-eligibility bridge lacks support. Let \(E_{ga,e}\) be projected CVAP exposure, \(w_{gac,e}\) its normalized complete-profile distribution, and \(\lambda_{gac,e}>0\) a count rate. Here \(g\) is a fine geographic support within event \(e\), whose key is jurisdiction/state, exact event date and counted-person universe. In the displayed reference, \(\lambda\) and \(T\) explicitly mean **counted participation**, in compatible person/event units; they do not receive another acceptance thinning:

\[
m_{gac,e}=E_{ga,e}w_{gac,e}\lambda_{gac,e},\qquad
U_e\mid\kappa_{\rm event}\sim\mathrm{Gamma}(\kappa_{\rm event},\mathrm{rate}=\kappa_{\rm event}),\qquad
T_{gac,e}\mid U_e,m\sim\mathrm{Poisson}(U_e m_{gac,e}).
\]

Conditional on \(U_e\) and the remaining states, these fine-cell counts are independent Poisson draws. With \(T_e=\sum_{g,a,c}T_{gac,e}\) and \(M_e=\sum_{g,a,c}m_{gac,e}\), integrating this one Gamma draw gives event mean \(M_e\) and variance \(M_e+M_e^2/\kappa_{\rm event}\), conditional on the remaining states. Distinct disjoint fine-cell counts have covariance \(m_i m_j/\kappa_{\rm event}\). One \(U_e\) multiplies every geographic/profile cell and is reused across all simultaneous office/report constraints. Refining geography or adding a district, office or report does not create another Gamma parent. Distinct event keys have distinct Gamma draws conditional on the shared per-arm \(\kappa_{\rm event}\), whose inherited prior is \(\log\kappa_{\rm event}\sim N(\log20,.75^2)\). Environmental and rate states retain their separately selected dependence.

This clarifies the already [selected event law](handoffs-20261009/downstream-joint-component-proposal-v3.md) and [geographic support requirement](handoffs-20261009/selected-full-cut-theorem-root-selection-v1.md). It replaces the earlier atom-local notation in this overview and the linked count reference; [pre-edit snapshots](handoffs-20261009/event-parent-clarification-v1/snapshot-manifest.json) preserve those bytes. Frozen experiments and their original targets remain unchanged. The [two-area arithmetic check](handoffs-20261009/root-geography-gamma-moment-check-v1.json) distinguishes the shared-event law from independent area frailties and premature geographic aggregation. Same-event offices additionally share the full participant-pattern table in section 7; sharing only \(U_e\) does not supply that dependence.

Use a hierarchical log-rate with demographic, community, place, event and community-by-place effects. Positive exposure is an offset, not a binomial trial count. This model supplies no eligible-conditional probability and no hard CVAP cap. Report excessive predictive tails and prior sensitivity; do not silently clip. Zero or missing exposure requires a coverage adapter, not an invented logarithmic offset.

