The full generative law defines each applicable joint ballot pattern: event status and each contest's participation, option and candidate category. Marginalize latent pattern counts subject to observed totals. On the exposure path, conditional on shared Gamma/environment states, pattern counts are Poisson thinnings with intensity times pattern probability. On the finite path they are multinomial within allocated profiles. This supplies a normalized joint likelihood even when only margins are observed.

The [district partial-observation reference](district-analysis-20261009/source-readiness/aggregate-observation-handoff-v1.md), with [independent review](district-analysis-20261009/source-readiness/aggregate-observation-independent-review-v1.md), exercises this law with unreported event/contest totals and different contest applicability. For disjoint constrained Poisson bins, the integrated Gamma denominator uses only their summed rates; unconstrained bins integrate out. Treating their counts as zero gives a different likelihood. The single-mark reference uses a binary incidence operator, whose columns can contain several ones across offices. The [finite-signature reference](district-analysis-20261009/source-readiness/partial-count-signature-reference-v1.md) and [root review](district-analysis-20261009/source-readiness/partial-count-signature-root-review-v1.md) extend the algebra to supplied binary matrices. Their independent-support convolution applies only to blocks with independent Gamma parents; geographic subdivisions of one selected event must retain one shared parent.

The newer [integer-multiplicity reference](constructive-review-20261009/historical-multimark-integer-reference-root-v1/README.md) and [bounded scientific audit](handoffs-20261009/historical-multimark-reference-response-scientific-audit-v1.md) support supplied nonnegative integer observation coefficients, including coarse write-in coefficients above one, with one Gamma parent per event. This small exact engine requires rational rates and a positive integer Gamma shape. The separately checked response kernel supplies normalized probabilities conditional on declared legal mark vectors and utilities. These checks do not authenticate actual legal support, join the response and observation components, qualify a real-valued-shape production backend, or pass the actual full-cut certificate.

The [real-valued-shape count reference](handoffs-20261009/historical-realshape-scientific-root-review-v1.md) now has bounded independent qualification for positive supplied pattern intensities, finite integer observation designs and their complete log-coordinate derivatives. It preserves one shared event parent, integrates invisible columns, and distinguishes impossible tables from resource exhaustion. Ten unique independent methods pass. Combinatorial preparation is not a national backend; actual source admission, complete pattern-rate construction, noisy F1a coupling and normalized downstream inference remain open.

The [same-table F1a reference](handoffs-20261010/event-report-composition-root-v1.md), with [independent confirmation](handoffs-20261010/event-report-composition-independent-review-v1.md), extends the count/report acceptance checks to shared event-Gamma counts and report shape 100. Candidate-invisible patterns still contribute to the table-derived participant total and hence the noisy report. Keep their conditional total distribution when marginalizing them; do not substitute candidate marks or an independent participant draw. Include the common release effect once across states. The exact conditional reference supplies a bounded probability sum, not production integration, derivative-error bounds or a full-cut certificate.

Single-contest reductions may be exact under declared conditioning. Multiplying all simultaneous contests' marginal likelihoods normally discards shared-ballot dependence. A composite or Gaussian aggregate approximation needs its own target label, cycle-level calibration, and exact-small-example comparison. The predictive sampler preserves common event parents.

Marginalize discrete classes where feasible; use independent initializations and forecast-functional convergence checks for continuous inference. Under a cut, each downstream draw remains conditioned on its actual upstream draw. Runtime problems do not justify removing unobserved uncertainty directions.

[Reference R4](model-stack-reference-models-20261009.md#r4-historical-totals-as-one-probability-model) supplies the normalized aggregate likelihood, exact small example and a latent-table augmentation backend with support-preserving integer moves. Its connectedness and runtime must be demonstrated on the actual observation matrix. The conditional-independent-office baseline defines a full ballot-pattern law but does not estimate residual ticket splitting; the CVR-dependent extension is a separate challenger.

Execution order is source admission → support/observation compilation → demographic fit → conditional community/measurement/behavior fit → future state/roster propagation → event and contest sampling → supported tabulation → immutable candidate-count artifact → derived shares. New polls create new runs rather than rewriting old forecasts.

**How to test:** compare exact small joint/cut calculations with each backend; test unchanged upstream marginals under protected policies, shared-event covariance and posterior predictive tail stability. Then freeze the empirical pipeline for the next election. A computational pass is not empirical qualification.

The [later same-table implementation review](constructive-review-20261009/event-table-report-independent-sol-v1/REVIEW.md), reconciled in the [v26 root disposition](handoffs-20261010/v26-inference-root-disposition-v1.md), qualifies a supplied complete-table density and continuous derivatives, not a table sampler or marginal likelihood. The [reviewed exact-signature proposal](handoffs-20261010/same-table-signature-inference-root-v1.md) permits a mathematically equivalent grouping only under complete identical factor signatures and one event owner, retaining the invisible participant total through F1a and conditionally reconstructing detailed counts. It selects no inference implementation. Visible-fiber connectivity and unbounded invisible-count handling remain required. The [per-parent normalization clarification](handoffs-20261010/per-parent-normalization-inference-clarification-independent-v1.md) preserves finite positive Z(U), unchanged protected masses and full-cut moment bounds; it explicitly does not require numerical Z(U) evaluation for a correct conditional MCMC method.

The [corrected grouped-prediction interface](handoffs-20261010/v27-grouped-prediction-interface-audit-v2.md) permits joint outputs from one shared conditional completion only under the stated likelihood-sufficiency conditions; detailed-table likelihoods require their tilted completion or augmented target. Full-output-signature grouping remains valid. The optional [factorized-rate computation](handoffs-20261010/v27-factorized-rate-computation-root-v1.md), with [independent algebra review](handoffs-20261010/v27-factorized-rate-computation-independent-review-v1.md), can construct grouped rates by finite polynomial convolution when complete signatures are additive across conditionally independent contest responses. It changes no raw support, prior, Gamma or report law and has no implementation/performance qualification. Actual generated-owner coupling, support-preserving numerical evaluation and frozen coefficient/derivative/resource tests remain required.

The [later compression and oracle disposition](handoffs-20261010/compression-rate-oracle-root-disposition-v1.md) accepts bounded build adoption of the supplied whole-output-signature reference and adds [executed exact coefficient/gradient evidence](handoffs-20261010/factorized-rate-oracle-independent-review-v1.md). A [separate independently differentiated normalization supplement](handoffs-20261010/factorized-normalization-supplement-independent-review-v1.md) resolves the first oracle's shared-helper validation gap. These finite invented references do not qualify an actual generated-rate producer, real response/profile-owner chain, floating-point implementation, arbitrary-real-shape sampler, F1a kernel or national feasibility. Their existing selected-law conditions and complete raw support remain mandatory.

