## 9. Experiments and acquisition

| Experiment | Frozen prediction | Next validation |
|---|---|---|
| Real reconstruction | Hidden raw and weighted joint tables from realistic published subsets | Reveal respondent records; compare raking/maximum entropy/rich-demographic baselines, interval coverage and error |
| Bridge transport | Missing associations using a declared overlap/glue sample | Withheld joint records, then new provider/wave; test beyond marginal balance |
| Dynamic communities | Later joint-answer distributions | New wave; compare prevalence, signature and segment-entry explanations |
| Community-by-place participation | Next event counts and supported subgroup probabilities | Recorded participation and official totals |
| Intention/approval transfer | Later responses under distinct kernels | Paired followup reports and later approval surveys |
| Joint ballots | Same-ballot ticket/rolloff patterns | Audited later CVRs, where available |
| Eligibility/exposure | Dated demographic and count forecasts | Compatible demographic/eligibility evidence and election counts |
| Sparse/no-poll transfer | Entire withheld provider/geography outcomes | Later releases and certified counts, including changed boundaries |
| Earlier behavioral signals | Next political wave and election counts | Prespecified as-of lags, compared against political/economic/demographic controls |
| Full stack | Every candidate, option and supported event total | Prespecified certified-result vintage, then separately dated supplements |

All tests freeze preprocessing, discovery, models, sources, roster and scores before the target. Specify numerical coverage/loss tolerances and minimum independent validation units before untouched evaluation. Multiple races sharing an election shock do not create independent cycle evidence. Report raw count error and scale-normalized comparisons, marginal and dependence-sensitive scores, and derived shares.

For new measurement, design a geographically stratified probability panel with joint affiliations/practices, intentions/approval and participation expectations; reinterview and add refreshment samples. Power the prespecified community-by-place contrasts after design effects/attrition rather than choosing a convenient fixed N. Consent/linkage can validate participation, not secret candidate choice.

Randomize invitation incentives/contact effort across the frame and wording among participants. A mode/crossover experiment also models order, time and selective response. Keep frame auxiliaries, dispositions and followup-subsample inclusion probabilities. Persistent nonresponders remain sensitivity-bounded. [Randomized-incentive research](https://www.nber.org/papers/w29549) and [mixed-mode experiment](https://academic.oup.com/jssam/article/7/4/545/5288348) provide relevant designs, not transferable coefficients.

Choose extra questions/crosstabs by expected reduction in prespecified composition/count uncertainty, considering cost and burden. Validate that selection rule on hidden real tables. More information is a testable opportunity; finite-sample forecast improvement is not guaranteed.

## 10. Remaining design and qualification gates

The [reference models and worked checks](model-stack-reference-models-20261009.md) now supply the dated exposure observation/projection model, numerical prior candidate, weighted-release likelihood, exact aggregate likelihood and constrained-count backend, ranked-ballot behavior/tabulation contract, and small source-to-count examples. This closes the corresponding design choices at reference-model level; it does not qualify them empirically or computationally at national scale.

1. **Prior qualification:** run full prior-predictive checks on real exposure/roster supports, select using earlier folds and freeze sensitivity before untouched evaluation.
2. **Observation/backend qualification:** verify weighted/rounded small cases and constrained aggregate sampling against exact references; demonstrate convergence and runtime on intended supports. Unsupported calibration/overlap cannot silently fall back to independent margins.
3. **Rules coverage:** implement and reconcile the [ranked-ballot contract](model-stack-reference-models-20261009.md#r5-ranked-ballots-and-dated-rules) against official fixtures. Other requested ballot regimes need their own authoritative adapters; a generic roster is insufficient.
4. **Input admission:** produce file-level harmonization/access/overlap receipts for actual sources; documented module names do not establish usable data intersections.
5. **End-to-end implementation:** exercise the complete selected route with an admitted input bundle. Independent reference-design review resolved its enumerated reference-law findings; the checked analytic examples establish arithmetic and probability semantics, not a fitted end-to-end forecast. The [selected ownership contract](handoffs-20261009/cut-contract-proposal.md) now resolves coordinate/factor/evidence ownership for eligibility, nuisance states and shared demographic/calibration information. Its empirical adapters, source admission and numerical qualification remain separate gates; see the [current handoff audit](handoffs-20261009/implementation-handoff-audit.md).

Empirical superiority and live publication remain downstream goals of the implementation program. Missing internal ground truth is handled through new measurements, bounds and qualified claims; it is not converted into an assertion that a latent explanation has been validated.

